2.1 Conditions Precedent. The obligations of the parties to consummate the Closing are subject to the fulfillment, at or prior to Closing, of the following conditions, unless waived by the party for whose benefit such condition exists:
(a) Receipt of all required governmental and third-party approvals and consents;
(b) Delivery of all required documents, instruments, and certificates, including but not limited to board resolutions and transfer documents;
(c) Accuracy of each party's representations and warranties at Closing;
(d) No material adverse change in the business, operations, or financial condition of the Company since the date hereof;
(e) No injunctions or legal restraints preventing Closing.

3.1 Representations and Warranties of the Seller. The Seller represents and warrants that:
(a) It has full power and authority to enter into and perform this Agreement;
(b) It is the sole legal and beneficial owner of the Shares, free and clear of all liens and encumbrances;
(c) The execution and delivery of this Agreement by the Seller do not conflict with any other agreement or obligation binding upon it;
(d) The financial statements provided to Buyer fairly present the financial position of the Company in all material respects and conform with generally accepted accounting principles.

